## 8. Performance Internals — Deep Dive

### 8.1 Clustering Score
- Ranges from **0.0** (completely unclustered) to **1.0** (perfectly clustered)
- Databricks recommends running OPTIMIZE when score drops below **0.5**
- `OPTIMIZE` is a no-op if score is already near 1.0

### 8.2 Target File Size
Liquid Clustering targets files of **~256MB to 1GB** (configurable).  
Larger files = fewer file opens = better scan performance.

```sql
ALTER TABLE sales_data
SET TBLPROPERTIES ('delta.targetFileSize' = '268435456'); -- 256MB in bytes
```

### 8.3 Z-Cube vs. Hilbert Cube
ZORDER uses a Z-curve. Liquid Clustering uses a **Hilbert curve**.

| Property | Z-Curve | Hilbert Curve |
|---|---|---|
| Locality | Moderate | **Better** |
| Number of "jumps" | More | **Fewer** |
| Query selectivity | Good | **Better** |
| Implementation complexity | Simpler | Higher |

